---
description: Gotchas when reading keyboard or gamepad input in browser code (KeyboardEvent, Gamepad API). Apply when writing input handling for web games, keyboard testers or controller testers.
alwaysApply: false
---

# Browser input handling

- Track keys by `event.code` (physical position), not `event.key`. Skip `event.repeat` when counting presses.
- Release every held key on `blur` and `visibilitychange`, and on Meta `keyup` (macOS drops other `keyup` events while Cmd is held).
- Fn never reaches the browser, and PrintScreen on Windows usually arrives as `keyup` only.
- Poll `navigator.getGamepads()` every animation frame. Don't keep `Gamepad` objects between frames, because Chromium returns new snapshots.
- Controllers stay hidden until a button is pressed, and the API needs HTTPS or localhost.
- Check `mapping === 'standard'` before trusting button and axis indexes. Read triggers from `buttons[6].value` and `buttons[7].value`.
- Don't claim to measure polling rate, latency or key actuation depth from browser events.
- For details, use the `browser-gamepad-input` and `browser-keyboard-testing` skills.
